41	56	345.STEP	uploads/orders/1776360562223_345.STEP	uploads/orders/conf_1776360562223_345.step	{"metal": {"id": 2, "faqs": [{"answer": "DMS Engineering offers 5052 H32 Aluminum in ten thickness options: .040'' (1.02mm), .063'' (1.60mm), .080'' (2.03mm), .090'' (2.29mm), .100'' (2.54mm), .125'' (3.18mm), .187'' (4.75mm), .250'' (6.35mm), .375''(9.5mm), .500'' (12.7mm).", "question": "What thicknesses does DMS Engineering offer 5052 H32 Aluminum in?"}, {"answer": "5052 H32 Aluminum is available at DMS Engineering with a range of thicknesses and part sizes. Instant quotes are possible for dimensions between .25'' x .375'' and 13'' x 44'', while custom quoting extends the maximum size to 13'' x 56''.", "question": "What are the minimum and maximum sizes for cutting 5052 H32 Aluminum?"}, {"answer": "You can add the following services to your 5052 H32 Aluminum parts: Anodizing, Bending, Deburring, Countersinking, Engraving, Dimple Forming, Hardware Insertion, Powder Coating, Tapping, and Tumbling", "question": "What additional services are available for 5052 H32 Aluminum?"}], "name": "5052 H32 ALUMINUM", "slug": "5052-h32-aluminum", "services": [1], "thickness": "11 thicknesses: .030\\" - .500\\"", "created_at": "2026-03-25T18:39:45.500Z", "image_path": "/uploads/metals/metal-1775556664125.webp", "quick_look": {"cutSizes": [{"size": ".25\\" x .375\\" min", "type": "solid", "label": "A", "action": "Instant Pricing"}, {"size": "30\\" x 44\\" max", "type": "solid", "label": "B", "action": "Instant Pricing"}, {"size": "30\\" x 56\\" max", "type": "outline", "label": "C", "action": "Custom Quote"}], "tolerance": "+/- .005\\"", "thicknesses": [{"value": ".040\\"", "metric": "1.02mm", "services": [1, 3, 5, 6]}, {"value": ".063\\"", "metric": "1.60mm", "services": [1, 8, 3, 9, 5, 6, 11, 7]}, {"value": ".080\\"", "metric": "2.03mm", "services": [1, 8, 3, 9, 5, 6, 11, 7]}, {"value": ".090\\"", "metric": "2.29mm", "services": [1, 8, 3, 9, 5, 6, 11, 7]}, {"value": ".100\\"", "metric": "2.54mm", "services": [1, 8, 3, 9, 5, 6, 10, 11, 7]}, {"value": ".125\\"", "metric": "3.18mm", "services": [1, 8, 3, 4, 9, 5, 6, 11, 7, 12]}, {"value": ".187\\"", "metric": "4.75mm", "services": [1, 8, 3, 4, 9, 6, 11, 7, 12]}, {"value": ".250\\"", "metric": "6.35mm", "services": [1, 8, 3, 4, 9, 6, 11, 7, 12]}, {"value": ".375\\"", "metric": "9.53mm", "services": [1, 8, 4, 9, 6, 11, 7, 12]}, {"value": ".500\\"", "metric": "12.7mm", "services": [1, 8, 4, 9, 6, 11, 7, 12]}, {"value": ".030\\"", "metric": "0.762mm", "services": []}]}, "updated_at": "2026-04-12T12:46:10.272Z", "category_id": 1, "description": "Excellent corrosion resistance, good weldability, and moderate strength.", "metal_level": true, "about_section": {"text": "5052 H32 aluminum is strong, inexpensive, and lightweight. Whether you're welding, machining, or bending, 5052 aluminum is going to be the go-to material for those projects that need excellent all-around material properties. Our laser cut 5052 aluminum is exceptionally lightweight and strong, making it perfect for projects where overall load is a concern.", "image": "/uploads/metals/about-metal-2.jpg", "title": "What is 5052 H32 Aluminum?", "capabilities": {"text": "With high relative ultimate strength (and fatigue strength), 5052 aluminum has a number of practical usages. It is non-heat treatable, which means that it is cold-worked to achieve its moderate-to-high strength properties. For greater strength, check out our 6061 series aluminum.", "items": ["Robotics", "Hinges", "Signage", "Fences", "Marine applications", "Panels", "Heat exchangers", "And so much more!"], "title": "What can you make with 5052 H32 Aluminum parts?"}, "featureChart": [{"label": "Strength", "rating": 3}, {"label": "Weldability", "rating": 4}, {"label": "Formability", "rating": 5}, {"label": "Heat Treating", "rating": 2}, {"label": "Corrosion Resistance", "rating": 5}, {"label": "Toughness", "rating": 4}, {"label": "Machinability", "rating": 3}, {"label": "Strength-t